{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1359527-what-murder-hobo-s-have-you-played-in-exalted","id":1359527,"title":"What Murder-Hobo's have you played in Exalted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-07T10:56:36-08:00","id":1359527,"title":"What Murder-Hobo's have you played in Exalted?","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/15221-the-new-adventures-of-spearpsycho-soulshitterson\">Tell me 'bout their great exploits.</a> They're kill counts. The tragic sadness of their tragedies. The joys of their happy slaughters. The over-kills beautifully stunted. How many hairs your Storytellers lost during your campaigns of justice...<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Munchkin_cat\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://openingofdoors.files.wordpress.com/2013/04/munchkin.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://1d4chan.org/images/a/ae/Murderhobo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 01-08-2020, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T18:01:12-08:00","id":1359614,"title":"","content":"In an old 2e game I ran, I had this whole arc planned out that kicked off with the main characters doing some favors for the Despot of Gem early on. But one of the players had a high-Conviction Righteous Devil Dawn. In his first meeting with the Despot, the poor mortal said something mildly irreverent to him and the Dawn slagged him and a good portion of the throne room, to the point that the molten stone was dripping into the floors below.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, another one of the Solars had - for reasons I don't remember - gotten himself into the city's reserves of firedust and accidentally set it all off. Luckily for him, he had the Resistance charms to survive the blast. Several blocks around him were not so luckily. The groups Midnight-masquerading-as-a-Zenith was happy to work on &quot;resolving&quot; the resulting shadowland. He didn't really do anything but it conveniently let him regen motes through later sessions.<br /> <br /> At that point, they decided that they might as well go all-in on their impromptu coup and took over the city, rather than be wandering heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","user":"Reminiscent Oasis","date":". 01-09-2020, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-07T21:18:33-08:00","id":1359643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1359527-what-murder-hobo-s-have-you-played-in-exalted?p=1359614#post1359614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an old 2e game I ran, I had this whole arc planned out that kicked off with the main characters doing some favors for the Despot of Gem early on. But one of the players had a high-Conviction Righteous Devil Dawn. In his first meeting with the Despot, the poor mortal said something mildly irreverent to him and the Zenith slagged him and a good portion of the throne room, to the point that the molten stone was dripping into the floors below.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, another one of the Solars had - for reasons I don't remember - gotten himself into the city's reserves of firedust and accidentally set it all off. Luckily for him, he had the Resistance charms to survive the blast. Several blocks around him were not so luckily. The groups Midnight-masquerading-as-a-Zenith was happy to work on &quot;resolving&quot; the resulting shadowland. He didn't really do anything but it conveniently let him regen motes through later sessions.<br /> <br /> At that point, they decided that they might as well go in on their impromptu coup and took over the city, rather than be wandering heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you break it you buy it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T01:53:05-08:00","id":1359669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1359527-what-murder-hobo-s-have-you-played-in-exalted?p=1359614#post1359614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an old 2e game I ran, I had this whole arc planned out that kicked off with the main characters doing some favors for the Despot of Gem early on. But one of the players had a high-Conviction Righteous Devil Dawn. In his first meeting with the Despot, the poor mortal said something mildly irreverent to him and the Zenith slagged him and a good portion of the throne room, to the point that the molten stone was dripping into the floors below.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, another one of the Solars had - for reasons I don't remember - gotten himself into the city's reserves of firedust and accidentally set it all off. Luckily for him, he had the Resistance charms to survive the blast. Several blocks around him were not so luckily. The groups Midnight-masquerading-as-a-Zenith was happy to work on &amp;quot;resolving&amp;quot; the resulting shadowland. He didn't really do anything but it conveniently let him regen motes through later sessions.<br /> <br /> At that point, they decided that they might as well go in on their impromptu coup and took over the city, rather than be wandering heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I ran a Gem game I headed that off by saying the Despot was wealthy enough that he could afford some seriously heavy duty guards. They still could have killed the whole throne room, but they weren't going to make it out unscathed.<br /> <br /> My players dont take shit from NPCs and will happily kill inconvenient characters.<br /> <br /> I had a player playing a shady Guild Caravaneer, and was trying to set up a deal with a corrupt spirit to play into and serve as a bit of a hook to move the story on to the next arc. Anyway, the party's Dawn was having none of this spirit's shit and cut him down in one blow. When the Guildsman objected and it can to blows, the Dawn, who was Melee superman, turned his daiklave on the guildsman dumped damn near every mote he had into a multi attack melee death combo an the Guildsman. The guildsman just barely survived because he was resistance supernal and surrendered because most of his big defenses had been shredded and couldn't be put back up.<br /> <br /> I dont really get to reuse npcs unless they are friendly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T02:33:51-08:00","id":1359672,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... My friend played a homeless teenager, but after he killed a man with one punch of a fist, he resolved to never fight again, so he was only really a murder-hobo briefly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T11:13:43-08:00","id":1359745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1359527-what-murder-hobo-s-have-you-played-in-exalted?p=1359672#post1359672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... My friend played a homeless teenager, but after he killed a man with one punch of a fist, he resolved to never fight again, so he was only really a murder-hobo briefly.</div> </div> </div> </div>characters like that tend to be far more interesting IMO<br /> <br /> ...namely because if you do it right, you can do a lot of things to people without killing them, especially with the right medical and/or mutation charms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T04:30:02-08:00","id":1360309,"title":"","content":"I've never played a murder hobo but I've gained greater appreciation for that type of character in light of how easy a lot of games make it no harder to play a character who just love taps everyone unconsious with their sword as the story groans under the weight of all the people they've taken captive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}